{
  "slug": "viv",
  "name": "Viv",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Turn Claude into a Viv expert. Design, develop, and debug code and content for Viv, a system for building simulated worlds where storylines emerge from character activity.\n\nViv offers technical narrative designers a custom programming language affording rich specifications of character actions, as well as constructs that drive *story sifting*—the task of identifying emergent storylines in a given simulation instance, such as a videogame playthrough.\n\nThis plugin maintains a synced copy of the Viv codebase, and bundles special commands for efficiently navigating it, allowing Claude to search the full language reference, compiler source, runtime source, and other material anytime it needs to look something up.\n\nSkills include `/setup` for fully automated Viv installation and project setup, `/write` for authoring Viv code from a brief, `/fix` for diagnosing compiler and runtime errors, `/design` for worldbuilding and architecture planning, and `/build` for writing integration code.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `ask` (Answer questions about Viv, an engine for emergent narrative), `build` (Write Viv integration code — adapters, test harnesses, simulation runners, runtime integrations), `critique` (Critique Viv code for optimization, clarity, emergent potential, and idiomatic style), `design` (Design Viv systems from a premise), `feedback` (Send feedback to the Viv team about the plugin, language, compiler, runtime, or documentation), `fix` (Diagnose and fix Viv errors), `setup` (Set up Viv in the current project), `study` (Deep-dive into Viv internals or the user's project), and 2 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `PreToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install viv@claude-community` from `siftystudio/viv` (`plugins/claude`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 10,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
